, "w": "accuracy"}, {"t": 13.326083, "d": 0.184791, "w": "went"}, {"t": 13.52175, "d": 0.304333, "w": "down"}, {"t": 14.152166, "d": 0.076083, "w": "the"}, {"t": 14.239125, "d": 0.217375, "w": "gap"}, {"t": 14.467375, "d": 0.358708, "w": "alone"}, {"t": 14.945666, "d": 0.260875, "w": "doesn't"}, {"t": 15.217375, "d": 0.184791, "w": "show"}, {"t": 15.413041, "d": 0.054333, "w": "an"}, {"t": 15.47825, "d": 0.489125, "w": "improvement"}, {"t": 16.326083, "d": 0.119583, "w": "Our"}, {"t": 16.456541, "d": 0.260875, "w": "best"}, {"t": 16.72825, "d": 0.380416, "w": "guess"}, {"t": 17.217375, "d": 0.086958, "w": "is"}, {"t": 17.315208, "d": 0.163041, "w": "that"}, {"t": 17.489125, "d": 0.163041, "w": "this"}, {"t": 17.663041, "d": 0.304333, "w": "small"}, {"t": 17.97825, "d": 0.369583, "w": "network"}, {"t": 18.402166, "d": 0.086958, "w": "on"}, {"t": 18.5, "d": 0.032625, "w": "a"}, {"t": 18.543458, "d": 0.336958, "w": "short"}, {"t": 18.891291, "d": 0.456541, "w": "recipe"}, {"t": 19.413041, "d": 0.282625, "w": "couldn't"}, {"t": 19.706541, "d": 0.260875, "w": "fit"}, {"t": 19.97825, "d": 0.065208, "w": "the"}, {"t": 20.054333, "d": 0.293458, "w": "harder"}, {"t": 20.358708, "d": 0.293458, "w": "data"}, {"t": 20.923916, "d": 0.097833, "w": "but"}, {"t": 21.032625, "d": 0.086958, "w": "we"}, {"t": 21.130416, "d": 0.184791, "w": "didn't"}, {"t": 21.326083, "d": 0.25, "w": "test"}, {"t": 21.586958, "d": 0.27175, "w": "that"}], "duration": 22.176708333333334, "spoken": "Then there's the gap between training and test accuracy, which went from about 7 points without augmentation to under 1 with crop plus flip. A smaller gap can mean useful regularization, or it can just mean the model learned less, and since test accuracy went down, the gap alone doesn't show an improvement. Our best guess is that this small network on a short recipe couldn't fit the harder data, but we didn't test that."}